391 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 806 0 R
/E (Learnings from Past Models: scMultiomeGRN and scTFBridge proved that integrating paired RNA and ATAC data is crucial for mapping physical regulation. However, both struggled with over-fitting and generalization due to noisy, mismatched, or computationally inferred validation baselines.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
392 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 807 0 R
/E (The Architecture \(MEvD-GRN\): Proposing a deliberately compact, dual-modality Graph Neural Network. It utilizes a "Gated Fusion" module to dynamically weigh RNA expression levels against ATAC chromatin accessibility, directly addressing the multi-omic sparsity problem.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
393 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 808 0 R
/E (Leveraging SC-MO-GRN-DB: Instead of just using the database for static benchmarking, we are using its tiered experimental data to drive Curriculum Learning. The model is trained sequentially from broad to strict biological evidence: Localization \(ChIP-seq\) -> Perturbation \(CRISPR/KO\) -> Dual-Evidence \(Intersection\).)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
394 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 809 0 R
/E (Hypotheses: By stepping the model from "easy/broad" binding data to "hard/strict" causal data, can we mathematically prevent the over-smoothing and generalization failures seen in previous GNN architectures? Can a lightweight model \(~125K parameters\) outcompete massive, computationally heavy baselines simply by utilizing a biologically smarter, evidence-aware training regimen?)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
